/** @page zipreleasenotesguide Release Notes

    @tableofcontents

    - Provide manifest-based uninstall and support CMake install-path normalization.
    - Detect the system Zstandard library through pkg-config when a distribution
      does not provide its CMake configuration. Preserve shared-library linking.

    @section zip_1_0 zip Module Version 1.0
    - Bundled minizip rejects overflowing memory-stream growth, safely resizes on reopen,
      and preserves archive comments when replacement validation or allocation fails
    - In-memory readers retain their input until closed, including temporary binary expressions
    - Debian/Ubuntu packages with offline minizip-ng 4.2.2, all compression and encryption features,
      source/AOT providers, compiler metadata, translations, API documentation, and debug symbols
    - Configurable private minizip-ng source directory; OpenSSL patch failures stop configuration
    - Initial release
    - Full ZIP64 support
    - Multiple compression methods (deflate, bzip2, lzma, zstd, xz)
    - Encryption: traditional PKWARE (ZipCrypto) by default for maximum interoperability with
      Windows Explorer, macOS Finder, and other common ZIP tools; optional AES-128/192/256 for
      strong encryption
    - \c ZIP-PASSWORD-ERROR raised cleanly when a password is required or incorrect, with no
      0-byte garbage left on disk
    - @ref Qore::Zip::ZipFile::extractAll() returns a @ref Qore::Zip::ZipExtractResult hash
      describing which entries were written and which were skipped because the destination
      already existed
    - @ref Qore::Zip::ZipFile::recompress() accepts an optional \c encryption_method
    - In-memory archive operations
    - Streaming API (@ref Qore::Zip::ZipInputStream / @ref Qore::Zip::ZipOutputStream)
    - Data provider module
    - @c qzip CLI with 11 commands and an \c -e / \c --encryption flag
